      AND COALESCE(d.metadata ->> 'source_recurrence_id', '') = ''
    LIMIT 1
),
updated_existing_event AS (
    UPDATE events
    SET
        title = '3D Character Workshop Series - Step 1: Hard Surface Modelling',
        description = '3D Character Series Overview 

Throughout this series, students will learn how to create, model, texture, rig, and animate 3D characters in Blender. Creating and animating 3D characters allows students to explore interests and careers in game development, animation, design, and VFX, among many others.  

The series consists of three steps: 1) Hard Surface Modelling, 2) Painted and Procedural Textures, and 3) Rigging and Animation. To complete the series, students should attend one session in each step. Each step has two session dates that students may select from based on their schedule. Students do not need to attend both dates for each step in order to complete the series.  

Students will be able to follow along with a member of the Spark staff using in-space computers.  

 

Step 1: Hard Surface Modelling 

Learn the basics of vertex editing to create low-poly models in Blender. Become familiar with Blender’s tools and functions in order to create basic shapes and meshes.  

 

Course Goals and Objectives 

By the end of this session, students will be able to: 

- Understand the various tools and functions of Blender, - Create and manipulate simple, low-poly meshes, and 

- Take home a simple humanoid mesh and static object mesh to use in Steps 2 and 3.',
        location_id = (SELECT location_id FROM resolved_location),
        start_date_time = TIMESTAMP '2026-03-30 10:00:00',
        end_date_time = TIMESTAMP '2026-03-30 12:00:00',
        event_type = 'Workshops & Training',
        status = 'SCHEDULED'::event_status,
        updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
    WHERE event_id IN (SELECT event_id FROM existing_event)
    RETURNING event_id
),
inserted_event AS (
    INSERT INTO events (
        title,
        description,
        location_id,
        start_date_time,
        end_date_time,
        event_type,
        status
    )
    SELECT
        '3D Character Workshop Series - Step 1: Hard Surface Modelling',
        '3D Character Series Overview 

Throughout this series, students will learn how to create, model, texture, rig, and animate 3D characters in Blender. Creating and animating 3D characters allows students to explore interests and careers in game development, animation, design, and VFX, among many others.  

The series consists of three steps: 1) Hard Surface Modelling, 2) Painted and Procedural Textures, and 3) Rigging and Animation. To complete the series, students should attend one session in each step. Each step has two session dates that students may select from based on their schedule. Students do not need to attend both dates for each step in order to complete the series.  

Students will be able to follow along with a member of the Spark staff using in-space computers.  

 

Step 1: Hard Surface Modelling 

Learn the basics of vertex editing to create low-poly models in Blender. Become familiar with Blender’s tools and functions in order to create basic shapes and meshes.  

 

Course Goals and Objectives 

By the end of this session, students will be able to: 

- Understand the various tools and functions of Blender, - Create and manipulate simple, low-poly meshes, and 

- Take home a simple humanoid mesh and static object mesh to use in Steps 2 and 3.',
        (SELECT location_id FROM resolved_location),
        TIMESTAMP '2026-03-30 10:00:00',
        TIMESTAMP '2026-03-30 12:00:00',
        'Workshops & Training',
        'SCHEDULED'::event_status
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM existing_event)
    RETURNING event_id
),
