updated_existing_event AS (
    UPDATE events
    SET
        title = 'Job Application Workshop: "Find It. Apply. Get Hired',
        description = 'Any major, any language -- join us! 

Bring your laptop and join our hands-on workshop!

 

Not sure where to find internships or jobs—or how to apply strategically? This workshop will show you how!

 

In this hands-on workshop organized by the Department of World Languages, students will meet the Director of Student Career Development, Dr. Jiyoung Yoon, and work with Career Center staff and a CLASS Career Coach to learn effective strategies for finding and applying for internships and jobs using platforms such as Handshake and LinkedIn.

 

With guidance from Career Center staff and a CLASS Career Coach, you’ll gain confidence navigating job boards, tailoring applications, and positioning your language skills as a competitive advantage.

 

✅ Learn where and how to search for opportunities
✅ Strengthen your application strategy
✅ Get personalized advice on next steps

 

Presenters:
Corey Davidson (Assistant Director, UNT Career Center)
Ryan Lorber (CLASS Career Coach)

 

Organizer and Facilitator:
Dr. Jiyoung Yoon, Professor of Spanish and Director of Student Career Development
Department of World Languages, Literatures, and Cultures

 

Attend even if you’re just starting to explore career options. Any major, any language—everyone is welcome!

 

📅 Date: Wednesday, April 15
⏰ Time: 3:00–4:30 PM
📍 Location: Curry Hall 203

 

Register here as soon as you can and save your spot! Job Application Workshop Registration

 

